respectively. Under each internal node is the covariate that is used to split the node.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="1471-2156-6-S1-S135-2"/></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>The 2 &#x000d7; 4 Table for root node</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td align="left">Response levels</td><td align="center">Node 2</td><td align="center">Node 3</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">1</td><td align="left">207</td><td align="left">54</td></tr><tr><td align="left">2</td><td align="left">21</td><td align="left">7</td></tr><tr><td align="left">3</td><td align="left">251</td><td align="left">157</td></tr><tr><td align="left">4</td><td align="left">199</td><td align="left">401</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T2"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>The identified SNPs</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td align="left">SNP label</td><td align="left">Trait<sup>a</sup></td><td align="left">Chromosome</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">rs930548</td><td align="left">A</td><td align="left">1</td></tr><tr><td align="left">rs628667</td><td align="left">A</td><td align="left">1</td></tr><tr><td align="left">rs1338221</td><td align="left">A</td><td align="left">1</td></tr><tr><td align="left">rs1840947</td><td align="left">A</td><td align="left">2</td></tr><tr><td align="left">rs1516003</td><td align="left">C</td><td align="left">2</td></tr><tr><td align="left">rs986909</td><td align="left">A</td><td align="left">3</td></tr><tr><td align="left">rs1599386</td><td align="left">A,C</td><td align="left">3</td></tr><tr><td align="left">rs319682</td><td align="left">A</td><td align="left">3</td></tr><tr><td align="left">rs728937</td><td align="left">A</td><td align="left">5</td></tr><tr><td align="left">rs1325182</td><td align="left">A</td><td align="left">6</td></tr><tr><td align="left">rs234</td><td align="left">A</td><td align="left">7</td>